.TH "LAGO" "1" "Sep 2026" "Lago CLI" "Lago CLI Manual"

.SH NAME
lago-v2-apply - Reconcile the product catalog with a folder of YAML files


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBlago v2 apply DIR [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Read every .yml and .yaml file under DIR and make the organization's product catalog match it: billable metrics, product categories, products, rate cards with their rates, and plans with their applied rate cards. Objects are matched by code. apply prints the plan first, then creates and updates in dependency order.

.PP
Pass --dry-run to print the plan without changing anything.

.PP
Nothing is deleted unless you pass --prune. apply records the objects it manages in a state file, DIR/.lago-state/\&.json by default; commit it with the YAML. --prune deletes the managed objects the files no longer declare, and never touches an object the folder did not create or adopt. The applied rate cards of a declared plan and the pending rates of a declared rate card belong to that object, so --prune also removes the ones the files dropped. Active and terminated rates are history and are kept. Deleting asks for confirmation; pass --confirm prune in scripts.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for apply

.PP
\fB--prune\fP[=false]
	Delete managed objects the files no longer declare

.PP
\fB--state\fP=""
	State file path (default DIR/.lago-state/\&.json)


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--api-key\fP=""
	Override the Lago API key

.PP
\fB--api-url\fP=""
	Override the Lago API URL

.PP
\fB--confirm\fP=""
	Confirm a dangerous operation with its resource identifier

.PP
\fB--dry-run\fP[=false]
	Print mutating requests without sending them

.PP
\fB--insecure\fP[=false]
	Allow insecure HTTP or TLS for self-hosted Lago

.PP
\fB--mode\fP=""
	Environment mode: live or test

.PP
\fB--no-retry\fP[=false]
	Disable automatic retries

.PP
\fB-o\fP, \fB--output\fP="table"
	Output format: table, json, or yaml

.PP
\fB--profile\fP=""
	Named profile to use

.PP
\fB--query\fP=""
	JMESPath expression applied to the response

.PP
\fB--timeout\fP=30s
	Total request timeout

.PP
\fB--timing\fP[=false]
	Print request latency breakdown

.PP
\fB--verbose\fP[=false]
	Print redacted request and response details


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  lago v2 apply billing/ --dry-run
  lago v2 apply billing/
  lago v2 apply billing/ --prune --confirm prune
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBlago-v2(1)\fP
